    "question": {
      ":question/id": "b5eb9141-9e63-5ade-9f13-ef07621b6313",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate ${\\int}_{C}\\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r}$ given that $\\mathbf{F}(x,y)=(- x + 2)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- y)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i}+(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t\\in[0,\\frac{\\pi}{2}].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r}=\\int_a^b \\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)},\\quad y=t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t)) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=(- x + 2)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(- y)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(- \\left(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) + 2\\right)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{} +\\left(- \\left(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}\\right)\\right)\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{} +(- t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{} +\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2)\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{} +(- t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} \\cdot\\left({\\begin{aligned}&(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{i} \\\\ &{} +(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + 2) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} +(- t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)}) \\\\ &{} \\cdot(- t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} + \\cos{\\left(t \\right)})\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=\\begin{aligned}&\\left({\\begin{aligned}&- t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\sin^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}  \\\\ &{} + 2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}}\\right) \\\\ &{} +\\left({t^{2} \\sin{\\left(t \\right)} \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - t \\cos^{2}{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right)\\end{aligned} \\\\ &=2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - t + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\int_C \\mathbf{F}\\cdot\\text{d}\\mathbf{r} \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\mathbf{F}(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot \\mathbf{r}^{\\prime}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}}\\left({2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - t + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ &=\\left[{- \\frac{t^{2}}{2} + 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}}\\right]_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\\\ &=(\\left(- \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{8}\\right)+(\\pi))-((0)+(0)) \\\\ &=(- \\frac{\\pi^{2}}{8} + \\pi)-(0) \\\\ &=\\frac{\\pi \\left(- \\pi + 8\\right)}{8}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$\n\nThe offset terms integrate by the reverse product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{gathered}\\frac{\\mathrm d}{\\mathrm dt}\\left(- \\frac{t^{2}}{2} + 2 t \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\right) \\\\ \\begin{aligned} &=2 t \\cos{\\left(t \\right)} - t + 2 \\sin{\\left(t \\right)}\\end{aligned}\\end{gathered}\n$$",
